Here's a detailed Minutes of Meeting (MOM) template for your year-end performance review:


---

Subject: Minutes of Meeting – Year-End Performance Review
Date: [Insert Meeting Date]
Attendees: [Your Name], [Manager's Name]
Duration: [Meeting Duration]


---

Agenda

1. Review key achievements and contributions.


2. Provide feedback on performance and areas of improvement.


3. Discuss development goals and career growth opportunities.


4. Share suggestions for team and process improvements.




---

Minutes

1. Achievements

Successfully delivered key projects, including:

ValpreAPI Library: Designed and implemented a robust library handling both Node.js and browser environments.

ValpreReactDataTable Component: Enhanced server-side rendering capabilities, streamlining data interactions.

CLI development for [specific project], improving project setup efficiency.


Contributed to optimizing microfrontend performance in Nx monorepo architecture.

Built user-friendly features such as the Document Preview Feature and People Hierarchy Component.

Maintained high code quality with 90%+ test coverage using Jest and contributed to compliance with organizational coding standards.



---

2. Feedback

Strengths:

Proactive in taking ownership of complex tasks and delivering high-quality solutions.

Strong technical expertise in React and microfrontend architecture.

Excellent collaboration with global teams and adherence to timelines.


Improvement Areas:

Enhance backend knowledge (Node.js, APIs) to contribute to full-stack development.

Improve time management and prioritization to handle multiple responsibilities effectively.




---

3. Development Goals

Gain expertise in backend technologies like Node.js and database handling.

Take ownership of a cross-team project in the next quarter.

Focus on system-wide architectural decisions for complex projects.



---

4. Career Growth Opportunities

Potential to transition into a Tech Lead role in the next 1-2 years by demonstrating leadership in larger projects.

Opportunities to mentor junior developers within the team.



---

5. Suggestions Shared

Proposed introducing bi-weekly technical sync-ups to improve collaboration and knowledge sharing within the team.

Suggested building a shared library of reusable components for internal use.



---

Outcomes

1. Action Items for You:

Enroll in a Node.js training program or take up backend-related tasks to improve skills.

Lead a major project in Q2 next year to demonstrate leadership capabilities.

Continue delivering high-quality work on UI/UX components and frameworks.



2. Action Items for the Team/Manager:

Start bi-weekly technical sync-ups from next quarter.

Explore the feasibility of creating a shared reusable component library.





---

Next Steps:

Schedule a check-in meeting in [specific month/quarter] to review progress on development goals.



